# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 5 of the Tutorial (Part 1)

[Bo2's Drill Exercise 3.2]

e,1,0,.1
r12,1,2,1'k
r2o,2,o,10'k
r30,3,0,1'k
r3o,3,o,20'k
o,3,2,o

analysis: dc
note: The op amp's power is negative, so it delivers 0.63 mW to the circuit rather than absorbing it.
rounding: 2
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Drill Exercise 3.11 (Thevenin)]

e,1,0,vs
r1,2,0,r1
r2,2,3,r2
o,1,2,3

analysis: dc
note: The chapter reaches for Thevenin / Norton here, which version 9 refuses outright: an ideal op amp has zero output resistance, so the short-circuit round divides by zero. A plain solve gets the same answer -- the Thevenin voltage of an unloaded output is the open-circuit node voltage, v3.
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


